# README/demo screenshots and the demo frames — the container never reads them.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket "*.png"/"*.gif"/"*.mp4". The app SERVES
# static/logo/*.png and static/pwa/*.png — the favicon, the header brand logo, and
# the PWA icons (app.py:352/369/1804-1806 and templates/index.html:6,7,11,1543
# reference them by path). A blanket rule silently stripped all eight out of the
# image, so Docker shipped with a broken favicon, a broken brand logo and no
# installable-app icon. The ! exceptions below put exactly those back, and they are
# written per-directory on purpose: "!static/**" would also re-include
# static/uploads/, which is deliberately excluded above as user data.
*.png
!static/logo/*.png
!static/pwa/*.png
*.gif
!static/logo/*.gif
!static/pwa/*.gif
*.mp4
!static/logo/*.mp4
!static/pwa/*.mp4